# Bring-up fallback only. Prefer IDpuLabVendorService API v2 in production.
# Values must be readable under both DAC and SELinux policy.

# Uncomment exactly one busy format for the target product. Leaving every line commented keeps
# the validated built-in candidates enabled. Qualcomm KGSL gpubusy is a per-window pair:
# gpu_busy_window=/sys/class/kgsl/kgsl-3d0/gpubusy
# Exynos Xclipse (AMD RDNA) direct percentage example:
# gpu_busy_percent=/sys/class/drm/card0/device/gpu_busy_percent
# Legacy/non-Xclipse Exynos Mali direct percentage:
# gpu_busy_percent=/sys/class/misc/mali0/device/utilization
# MediaTek direct percentage is built in when readable:
# gpu_busy_percent=/sys/module/ged/parameters/gpu_loading
# Strict MediaTek "loading blocking idle" product path, if deliberately exposed:
# gpu_busy_mtk_triplet=/sys/vendor/path/to/ged_gpu_utilization

# Choose exactly one typed unit key. This placeholder example node reports kHz.
# gpu_frequency_khz=/sys/vendor/path/to/gpu_cur_freq_khz
# MediaTek "<OPP index> <frequency kHz>" product path:
# gpu_frequency_index_khz=/sys/vendor/path/to/current_freqency
# bus_busy=/sys/vendor/path/to/ddr_busy
# dpu_busy=/sys/vendor/path/to/dpu_active_percent
# Explicit unit contract: this value must be Hz.
# dpu_frequency_hz=/sys/vendor/path/to/dpu_cur_freq_hz
# dpu_underrun=/sys/vendor/path/to/dpu_underrun_count
